From 9d7a7cc7016c9413abcc02c2922c58768abec289 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:36:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix recurring 422 on improvement proposals at the root cause

The 422 kept coming back because each earlier PR only nudged one limit
(findings required -> summary 1600 -> summary 6000) while the clients and
inputs that feed the endpoint did not match the API's bounds:

- studio.js sends up to 10000 chars of specialist context, but
  visual_summary was capped at 6000 -> 422 on any real multi-specialist run.
- ImprovementFinding was strictly bounded/min_length=1 while the inspector's
  VisualFinding is unbounded and vision models can emit any severity, so long
  or empty fields and e.g. "critical" severity were rejected.
- Clients threw Error(detail) with FastAPI's array detail, showing
  "[object Object]" so the real cause was invisible.

Changes:
- Raise visual_summary to 10000 (matches clients) and trim instead of reject;
  keep a 100k hard ceiling. Normalize/trim finding fields and severity.
- Add formatApiError() and use it on every client error path.
- Reject empty path segments in scope validation (doubled Windows separators).
- Fix stale/incorrect tests that were already failing on main: literal "\\n"
  base64 fixture, missing git tree stub, and an under-sized summary fixture
  (1082 chars asserted > 1600) that never exercised the bug.
- Add regression tests incl. an API-level test that fails with 422 on the
  old code.
